  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save Her Seat (SHS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&#x2019;s ultimate objective is to increase access to, and quality of education for 4,800 vulnerable girls in grades- 5-7, including 150 girls with disabilities, through creating a continuous pathway for girls to stay in school longer, learn more and better, and increase transition rates to secondary school. Save Her Seat (SHS) will be implemented in 40 primary schools across the Tarime and Serengeti districts of Northern Tanzania. Additionally, 120 teachers and 33 Education Officials will benefit from training and support provided through the project, with over 6,000 community members indirectly benefitting through involvement in community engagement and sensitization activities.</narrative>
  </description>
