  <document-link format="APPLICATION/PDF" url="https://iatipublisher-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/document-link/36/Baseline_Study_and_Gender_Context_Analysis_Report_RTP_Save_Her_Seat_296_Submitted1707335132.pdf">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save Her Seat Baseline Evaluation</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Save Her Seat project is a 3-year project (April 2023 &#x2013; April 2026) funded by the Foreign, 
Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO) and the Liverpool Football Club Foundation (LFCF) . 
In the long-term, Save Her Seat will contribute to increasing the promotion of gender equality and 
improved learning outcomes for girls in grades 5 &#x2013; 7 through the provision of quality education in 
Tanzania. Within the next three years, the project aims to increase retention, attendance rates and 
life skills among 4,800 girls in grades 5 - 7 (approx. 12 &#x2013; 15 years old) in 40 primary schools in Tarime 
and Serengeti districts. The project will target girls in grade 5 to 7 as they are more at risk of dropping 
out of school. 

We are seeking to procure the services of an independent consultant/consultant team to lead and codesign the baseline and gender context analysis (July 2023) and endline evaluation (January 2026) for 
the Save Her Seat project with Right To Play. The overall objective of the baseline will be to provide 
contextual information on the current conditions of education for girls in the Mara region by using a 
participatory and collaborative approach.</narrative>
   </description>
